From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VU1 interpreter: lane loops unrolled on GCC/Clang; commit check inline in loopHead

What it is for:
  At -O2 GCC keeps the executors' and FMAC model's 4-lane loops as loops,
  so in translated code (constant dest mask) each lane's dest test and
  each operand normalisation still ran. And loopHead called the commit
  pass before every pair, although after patch 0028 that pass rarely has
  work and its call costs more than its own early exit.

The change:
  - PS2_VU_UNROLL_LANES (`#pragma GCC unroll 4` on GCC, `#pragma unroll 4`
    on Clang, nothing on MSVC, which unrolls these at /O2) before the 4-lane
    loops of the upper executor and the FMAC model.
  - loopHead checks m_cycle >= m_nextCommitCycle before calling
    commitReadyPipelines (the same condition as its early exit).
  Same results. Tested: ps2xTest 454/454; the Ben 10 port's 40 captured
  VU1 workloads give the same checksums and cycle count with and without
  its translated code; translated code 214 M -> 184 M instructions.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vu1.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vu1.h
@@ -20,6 +20,18 @@
 #define PS2_VU_FORCEINLINE inline __attribute__((always_inline))
 #endif
 
+// The 4-lane loops of the executors and the FMAC model, fully unrolled on
+// GCC and Clang (-O2 keeps them as loops): with a translated word's
+// constant dest mask the per-lane tests then fold away (findings/21 s.16).
+// MSVC has no unroll pragma; it unrolls such loops on its own at /O2.
+#if defined(__clang__)
+#define PS2_VU_UNROLL_LANES _Pragma("unroll 4")
+#elif defined(__GNUC__)
+#define PS2_VU_UNROLL_LANES _Pragma("GCC unroll 4")
+#else
+#define PS2_VU_UNROLL_LANES
+#endif
+
 // The FMAC result and flag model (runtime/ps2_vu1_fmac_inl.h), forced inline.
 // Translated code compiles one opcode case per upper word (execUpperT), so
 // each copy of the model is for one instruction. (Before that, MSVC inlined
@@ -634,7 +646,8 @@
 {
     if (!(m_cycle < f.budgetEnd && !m_stopRequested))
         return StepResult::Break;
-    commitReadyPipelines();
+    if (m_cycle >= m_nextCommitCycle) // its own early exit, checked here
+        commitReadyPipelines();
     if (m_state.pc + 8u > f.codeSize)
         return StepResult::Break;
     return StepResult::Continue;
